# {{ .name }}

An Intropy job. Each run calls `Job.ExecuteAsync` once, inside one span
named after the component, then exits with `0` (success), `1` (the job
failed) or `2` (the Dapr sidecar was unavailable). In production it runs as a
CronJob; the schedule is deployment configuration.

## How a run flows

```
scheduled run (CronJob)
   │
   ▼
JobRunner waits for the Dapr sidecar ──▶ not available ──▶ exit 2
   │
   ▼
Job.ExecuteAsync ──▶ throws, or reports Failed > 0 ──▶ exit 1
   │
   ▼
RunSummary (processed / failed / skipped) ──▶ exit 0
```

SIGTERM or Ctrl+C cancels the run, which exits 0 and leaves the remaining
work for the next run, so a run must be safe to repeat.

## Build and test

```bash
task build
task test
```

## Container image

From the system folder (the parent of this one):

```bash
docker build -f {{ .appId }}/Dockerfile -t {{ .appId }} .
```

